<[Deano] D.MARTINDAL1> before i knew much about forth...
<[Gary] GARY-S> It is more ordinary to have 2 or 3 going simultaneously on 
FIGGY nights
<[Deano] D.MARTINDAL1> i implemented it on my one-time Commodore 128
<[Gary] GARY-S> what are you driving now , still the C-128 ?
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> did you start from scratch or convert an exisiting system?
<[Deano] D.MARTINDAL1> now have 286 epson
<[Deano] D.MARTINDAL1> from scratch, starting forth, and 83 standard
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> congrats, few have gone that far
<[Deano] D.MARTINDAL1> on the surface it looked pretty good...
<[Deano] D.MARTINDAL1> but later I learned how inefficient my internals were
<[Gary] GARY-S> did you do the inner interpreter in assembler
<[Deano] D.MARTINDAL1> but of course
<[Gary] GARY-S> then what was the prob ?
<[Deano] D.MARTINDAL1> checked for stack under/overflow with each access...
<[Deano] D.MARTINDAL1> jsr's instead of jumps for calling code words
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> is anyone ever finished tweeking Forth's internals?
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> there are so many ways to do it, you are never done 
experimenting
<[Gary] GARY-S> still - sounds like you did a commendable job
<[Deano] D.MARTINDAL1> hank you
<[Deano] D.MARTINDAL1> 't'hank you
<[Gary] GARY-S> I also accept hanks :-)
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> what you using on the epson now?
