<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> good enough, and can understand why you want to write your 
own :-)
<[Gary] GARY-S> Have you looked at bbl and pygmy - two other extremes
<[Deano] D.MARTINDAL1> fg-pc has good parts, parts I don't care for
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> ah, a classic Forth programmer <grin>
<[Deano] D.MARTINDAL1> did not succeed in finishing my pc 4th yet
<[Deano] D.MARTINDAL1> have not looked at bbl & pygmy
<[Gary] GARY-S> pygmy is a VERY minimal Forth for dos..
<[Gary] GARY-S> bbl is a split header 32 bit forth and fast as hell !
<[Deano] D.MARTINDAL1> must check them out
<[Deano] D.MARTINDAL1> that's one thing I don't like about f-pc...
<[Deano] D.MARTINDAL1> TOO big
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> Yea!
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> you might also look at ZEN if you like small
<[Gary] GARY-S> caveat - BBL comes with a HUMONGOUS business language called 
Abundance. Try to get just BBL if possible
<[Deano] D.MARTINDAL1> like uncluttered more than small, so i can build to my 
liking
<[Gary] GARY-S> I don't care for that fat a kernel either (f-pc)
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> we do have BBL sans Abundance in the library
<[Gary] GARY-S> VERY FAST !!!!!!!
<[Deano] D.MARTINDAL1> source on any of these available?
<[Gary] GARY-S> all of them
