<[Deano] D.MARTINDAL1> I know it wasn't jax--him i would have remembered
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> Martin's article on masm and Forth was written around ZEN
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> what type of threading are you doing in your pc 4th?
<[Deano] D.MARTINDAL1> indirect
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> not the fastes, but easier to think about
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> is it a 64K model?
<[Deano] D.MARTINDAL1> split up into code seg, forth seg, data seg, header seg, 
buffer seg
<[Deano] D.MARTINDAL1> with (obviously) max of 64K each
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> very nice
<[Deano] D.MARTINDAL1> except for buffer, which is unlimited
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> I assume only one file buffer
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> is that right?
<[Deano] D.MARTINDAL1> file buffer, but not one
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> how many?
<[Deano] D.MARTINDAL1> dynamically allocated, as loads call files
<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> is buffer allocated until you run out of memory
<[Deano] D.MARTINDAL1> yes, memory you have assigned to the buffer, anyway
